<h3 class="storytitle" id="post-21"><a href="http://www.marksportal.net/blog/index.php?p=21" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: The Great Mountain of God">The Great Mountain of God</a></h3>


		
		<!-- Actual post -->
<div class="storycontent">
	<p>As I was reading the Bible today I was reminded of some inspiriational words that Paul wrote down in Hebrews.   The imagery he describes tends to lift my spirit up.</p>
	<p><em>&#8220;<b>You have not come</b> to a mountain that can be touched and that is burning with fire; to darkness, gloom and storm; to a trumpet blast or to such a voice speaking words that those who heard it begged that no further word be spoken to them, because they could not bear what was commanded:  &#8216;If even an animal touches the mountain, it mus be stoned.&#8217;  The sight was so terrifying that Moses said, &#8216;I am trembling with fear.&#8217;&#8221;(Hebrews 12:18-21, NIV)</em></p>
	<p>Paul is describing what the Israelites saw when God came down on Mount Sinai and spoke to them.  God had just brought the Israelites out of Egypt, using Moses as His spokesman, and Moses brought them to Mount Sinai as God had instructed him<em>(Exodus 3:12)</em>.  As they were gathering God came down onto the mountain and fear struck everyone, as was described above and in Exodus 19:16-20.  It was terrifying and they all shook with fear.   In fact, it was so frightening that they cried out to Moses, <em>&#8220;Speak to us yourself and we will listen.  But do not have God speak to us or we will die.&#8221;(Exodus 20:19)</em>   That&#8217;s the mountain that the Israelites came to, but Paul goes on&#8230;</p>
	<p><em>&#8220;<b>But you have come</b> to Mount Zion, to the heavenly Jerusalem, the city of the living God.  You have come to thousands upon thousands of angels in joyful assembly, to the church of the firstborn, whose names are written in heaven.  You have come to God, the judge of all men, to the spirits of righteous men made perfect, to Jesus the mediator of a new covenant, and to the sprinked blood that speaks a better word than the blood of Abel.&#8221; (Hebrews 12:22-24, NIV)</em></p>
	<p>Today when we pray or worship God we do not do so at Mount Sinai, we worship God in a MUCH more frightening place&#8230;.Mount Zion, God&#8217;s holy mountain.  As soon as we start to pray or worship God, our spirit stands before God on His holy mountain.   Re-read the above verses again.  You haven&#8217;t come to just a mountain of smoke and fire.  When you pray you are standing before the very throne of the living God.  You are surrounded by &#8220;thousands upon thousands of angels&#8221;.  You stand in the presence of &#8220;the spirits of righteous men made perfect&#8221;.   I am reminded of the words of Solomon:</p>
	<p><em>&#8220;Guard your steps when you go to the house of God.  Go near to listen rather than to offer the sacrifice of fools, who do not know that they do wrong.  Do not be quick with your mouth,  do not be hasty in your heart to utter anything before God.   God is in heaven and you are on earth, so let your words be few.&#8221; (Ecclesiastes 5:1-2, NIV)</em></p>
	<p>After Paul describes the frightening scene of Mount Sinai and then the terrifying view of Mount Zion he gives a warning. </p>
	<p><em>&#8220;See to it that you do not refuse him who speaks.&#8221; (Hebrews 12:25, NIV)</em></p>
	<p>&#8220;Listen to God and do what He says&#8221;, Paul warns.  Above, Paul describes two terrifying scenes and gives us a warning.  Yet there is also GREAT encouragement to be had in reading those scenes.   Did you see who dwells on God&#8217;s holy mountain?  Here is the list:  </p>
	<p>God<br />
Jesus<br />
&#8220;thousands upon thousands of angels&#8221;<br />
&#8220;spirits of righteous men made perfect&#8221;.</p>
	<p>When you pray and worship be comforted that you are surrounded by MANY others.   Those who have walked with God in the past and those who walk with Him in the present.  You are &#8220;surrounded by a great cloud of witnesses&#8221;.   Let me end this with some of Paul&#8217;s encouraging words:</p>
	<p><em>&#8220;Therefore, since we are surrounded by such a great cloud of witnesses, let us throw off everything that hinders and the sin that so easily entagles, and let us run with perseverance the race marked out for us. &#8221; (Hebrews 12:1, NIV)</em></p>
